# API Design Document (ADD)
## Indian Wedding Management Platform — MERN Stack

**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Initial API Specification
**Frontend:** React.js + Vite
**Backend:** Node.js + Express.js
**Language:** JavaScript (ES Modules)
**Database:** MongoDB Atlas
**ODM:** Mongoose
**Validation:** Zod
**Authentication:** JWT + HttpOnly Cookies
**Architecture:** Modular Monolith
**API Style:** REST API
**Base URL:** `/api/v1`

---

# 1. API Overview

## 1.1 Objective

The API layer handles communication between the React frontend and backend business logic.

It provides endpoints for:

- User authentication.
- User profile management.
- Wedding workspace management.
- Wedding member management.
- Manager invitations.
- Wedding event management.
- Guest management.
- Gallery management.
- Public wedding website access.
- Public gallery access.
- Workspace activity tracking.

## 1.2 API Architecture

The application follows a Modular Monolith architecture.

The frontend and backend are separate applications. All backend modules run inside one Express application while maintaining separate business logic.

```text
React Frontend
      |
      v
React Router
      |
      v
Axios API Client
      |
      v
Express API Routes
      |
      v
Authentication Middleware
      |
      v
Authorization Middleware
      |
      v
Validation Middleware
      |
      v
Module Controllers
      |
      v
Service Layer
      |
      v
Mongoose Models
      |
      v
MongoDB Atlas
```

## 1.3 Backend API Folder Structure

```text
backend/
└── src/
    ├── config/
    │   ├── database.js
    │   ├── cloudinary.js
    │   └── environment.js
    │
    ├── middlewares/
    │   ├── auth.middleware.js
    │   ├── membership.middleware.js
    │   ├── role.middleware.js
    │   ├── validate.middleware.js
    │   ├── rateLimit.middleware.js
    │   └── error.middleware.js
    │
    ├── modules/
    │   ├── auth/
    │   │   ├── auth.routes.js
    │   │   ├── auth.controller.js
    │   │   ├── auth.service.js
    │   │   └── auth.validation.js
    │   │
    │   ├── users/
    │   ├── weddings/
    │   ├── members/
    │   ├── invitations/
    │   ├── events/
    │   ├── guests/
    │   ├── gallery/
    │   ├── public-access/
    │   └── audit-logs/
    │
    ├── utils/
    │   ├── ApiError.js
    │   ├── ApiResponse.js
    │   ├── asyncHandler.js
    │   ├── token.js
    │   └── permissions.js
    │
    ├── routes/
    │   └── index.js
    │
    ├── app.js
    └── server.js
```

Each feature module follows:

```text
events/
├── event.model.js
├── event.routes.js
├── event.controller.js
├── event.service.js
└── event.validation.js
```

---

# 2. API Standards

## 2.1 HTTP Methods

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| GET | Retrieve resources |
| POST | Create resources or perform actions |
| PATCH | Update specific fields |
| PUT | Replace a complete resource |
| DELETE | Delete or revoke resources |

## 2.2 Response Format

All API responses follow a consistent structure.

### Success Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Wedding created successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": "wedding_object_id",
    "title": "Rahul & Priya Wedding"
  }
}
```

### Error Response

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "You are not authorized to access this wedding",
  "error": {
    "code": "FORBIDDEN"
  }
}
```

## 2.3 HTTP Status Codes

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 200 | Successful request |
| 201 | Resource created |
| 204 | Successful deletion without response body |
| 400 | Invalid request |
| 401 | Authentication required |
| 403 | Permission denied |
| 404 | Resource not found |
| 409 | Resource conflict |
| 422 | Validation failed |
| 429 | Too many requests |
| 500 | Internal server error |

## 2.4 Pagination

List APIs support pagination.

Example:

```http
GET /api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/events?page=1&limit=10
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": [],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "total": 45,
    "totalPages": 5
  }
}
```

Requirements:

- Default page: 1.
- Default limit: 10.
- Maximum limit: 100.
- Validate pagination parameters on the backend.

## 2.5 API Versioning

All endpoints use:

```text
/api/v1
```

Future breaking API changes can be introduced through a new version.

---

# 3. Authentication APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/auth`

Authentication APIs manage registered users and JWT sessions.

## 3.1 Signup

**POST** `/auth/signup`

Purpose: Register a new user.

Request:

```json
{
  "name": "Rahul Singh",
  "email": "rahul@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPassword123"
}
```

Response — `201 Created`:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Account created successfully",
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "id": "user_object_id",
      "name": "Rahul Singh",
      "email": "rahul@example.com",
      "isEmailVerified": false,
      "status": "ACTIVE"
    }
  }
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Validate request using Zod.
2. Check whether email already exists.
3. Hash password using bcrypt.
4. Create user.
5. Establish an authenticated session.
6. Return safe user information.

## 3.2 Login

**POST** `/auth/login`

Request:

```json
{
  "email": "rahul@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPassword123"
}
```

Response — `200 OK`:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login successful",
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "id": "user_object_id",
      "name": "Rahul Singh",
      "email": "rahul@example.com"
    }
  }
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Validate email and password.
2. Find user by email.
3. Verify password using bcrypt.
4. Check account status.
5. Generate JWT.
6. Set JWT in an HttpOnly cookie.

The JWT must not be returned in the response body when using cookie-based authentication.

## 3.3 Logout

**POST** `/auth/logout`

Authentication: Required.

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Logout successful"
}
```

The authentication cookie will be cleared using matching cookie options.

## 3.4 Get Current User

**GET** `/auth/me`

Authentication: Required.

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": "user_object_id",
    "name": "Rahul Singh",
    "email": "rahul@example.com"
  }
}
```

---

# 4. User APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/users`

## 4.1 Get Profile

**GET** `/users/me`

Authentication: Required.

Returns the authenticated user's profile.

## 4.2 Update Profile

**PATCH** `/users/me`

Authentication: Required.

Request:

```json
{
  "name": "Rahul Kumar",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "avatar": "https://example.com/avatar.jpg"
}
```

Only allowed profile fields can be updated.

## 4.3 Delete Account

**DELETE** `/users/me`

Authentication: Required.

Account deletion must consider existing wedding ownership and membership relationships.

An ADMIN cannot simply delete their account while leaving a workspace without a valid administrator.

---

# 5. Wedding Management APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings`

These APIs manage wedding workspaces.

## 5.1 Create Wedding

**POST** `/weddings`

Authentication: Required.

Request:

```json
{
  "title": "Rahul & Priya Wedding",
  "couple": {
    "partnerOne": "Rahul",
    "partnerTwo": "Priya"
  },
  "weddingDate": "2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z",
  "location": {
    "venue": "Royal Palace",
    "city": "Bhopal",
    "state": "Madhya Pradesh",
    "country": "India"
  },
  "settings": {
    "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata",
    "currency": "INR",
    "language": "en"
  }
}
```

Response — `201 Created`:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Wedding created successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": "wedding_object_id",
    "title": "Rahul & Priya Wedding",
    "status": "PLANNING",
    "role": "ADMIN"
  }
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Authenticate user.
2. Validate request.
3. Generate a unique slug.
4. Create wedding.
5. Create ADMIN membership.
6. Execute both database operations in a MongoDB transaction.
7. Return the created wedding.

## 5.2 Get All User Weddings

**GET** `/weddings`

Authentication: Required.

Returns all weddings where the authenticated user has ACTIVE membership.

## 5.3 Get Wedding Details

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId`

Authentication: Required.

Authorization:

- User must have ACTIVE membership.
- ADMIN and MANAGER can access workspace details.

## 5.4 Update Wedding

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId`

Authentication: Required.

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Request:

```json
{
  "title": "Rahul & Priya Wedding Celebration",
  "description": "Our wedding celebration",
  "location": {
    "city": "Indore"
  }
}
```

Only explicitly allowed fields can be updated.

## 5.5 Delete Wedding

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId`

Authentication: Required.

Permission: ADMIN only.

Deletion must follow the wedding data lifecycle policy.

The initial implementation should prefer archival through `status: "ARCHIVED"` rather than immediate permanent deletion.

---

# 6. Wedding Member APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/members`

These APIs manage workspace membership.

## 6.1 Get All Members

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/members`

Permission: ACTIVE ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 6.2 Get Member Details

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/members/:memberId`

Permission: ACTIVE ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 6.3 Approve Membership Request

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/members/:memberId/approve`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Membership approved successfully"
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Verify ADMIN authorization.
2. Find membership belonging to the requested wedding.
3. Verify membership is PENDING.
4. Update status to ACTIVE.
5. Record `approvedBy` and `joinedAt`.
6. Update related invitation status where applicable.

## 6.4 Reject Membership Request

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/members/:memberId/reject`

Permission: ADMIN only.

## 6.5 Update Member Role

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/members/:memberId/role`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Request:

```json
{
  "role": "MANAGER"
}
```

Only supported workspace roles can be assigned.

## 6.6 Remove Member

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/members/:memberId`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Rules:

- ADMIN cannot remove the sole administrator.
- Historical audit records must be preserved.
- Removed users must lose access immediately.

---

# 7. Manager Invitation APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/invitations`

These APIs manage manager invitations.

## 7.1 Create Invitation

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/invitations`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Request:

```json
{
  "email": "manager@example.com"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Invitation created successfully"
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Verify ADMIN permissions.
2. Validate email.
3. Check for an existing active invitation or membership.
4. Generate a cryptographically random token.
5. Hash token.
6. Store token hash in MongoDB.
7. Set expiration.
8. Send invitation link through email.

## 7.2 Get Invitations

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/invitations`

Permission: ADMIN only.

## 7.3 Revoke Invitation

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/invitations/:invitationId`

Permission: ADMIN only.

## 7.4 Validate Invitation

**GET** `/invitations/:token`

Authentication: Not required.

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "weddingTitle": "Rahul & Priya Wedding",
    "email": "manager@example.com",
    "status": "PENDING",
    "expiresAt": "2027-01-15T00:00:00.000Z"
  }
}
```

The response must not expose the token hash or internal invitation credentials.

## 7.5 Accept Invitation and Submit Membership Request

**POST** `/invitations/:token/accept`

Authentication: Required.

Request:

```json
{
  "confirm": true
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Validate invitation token.
2. Check expiration and revocation.
3. Verify authenticated user's email matches invited email.
4. Check for existing membership.
5. Create PENDING membership.
6. Update invitation status to ACCEPTED.
7. Wait for ADMIN approval.

Accepting an invitation does not automatically grant workspace access.

---

# 8. Event Management APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/events`

These APIs manage wedding ceremonies.

## 8.1 Create Event

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/events`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Request:

```json
{
  "name": "Haldi Ceremony",
  "description": "Traditional Haldi celebration",
  "date": "2027-02-13T00:00:00.000Z",
  "startTime": "10:00",
  "endTime": "13:00",
  "venue": {
    "name": "Royal Palace",
    "address": "Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh"
  },
  "visibility": "PUBLIC"
}
```

## 8.2 Get All Events

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/events`

Permission: ACTIVE ADMIN or MANAGER.

Query parameters:

```http
?page=1&limit=10&status=UPCOMING&sortBy=date&order=asc
```

## 8.3 Get Event Details

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/events/:eventId`

Permission: ACTIVE ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 8.4 Update Event

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/events/:eventId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 8.5 Delete Event

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/events/:eventId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Before deleting an event, the backend must handle its references in guest and gallery records.

---

# 9. Guest Management APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/guests`

Guests do not require authentication or user accounts.

These management APIs are accessible only to authorized workspace members.

## 9.1 Add Guest

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Request:

```json
{
  "name": "Amit Sharma",
  "email": "amit@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "familyGroup": "Sharma Family",
  "side": "GROOM",
  "eventIds": [
    "event_object_id_1",
    "event_object_id_2"
  ]
}
```

Every referenced event must belong to the same wedding.

## 9.2 Get All Guests

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Query parameters:

```http
?page=1&limit=20&side=GROOM&search=Amit
```

## 9.3 Get Guest Details

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests/:guestId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 9.4 Update Guest

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests/:guestId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 9.5 Delete Guest

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests/:guestId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 9.6 Bulk Import Guests

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/guests/bulk`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Purpose:

- Import multiple guests.
- Validate individual guest records.
- Associate guests with wedding events.
- Return successful and failed records.

Bulk imports should have a configured maximum record count and clear partial-failure reporting.

---

# 10. Gallery Management APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/gallery`

These APIs manage photographs and videos.

Actual media files are stored in Cloudinary. MongoDB stores media metadata.

## 10.1 Get Gallery Assets

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery`

Permission: ACTIVE ADMIN or MANAGER.

Query parameters:

```http
?page=1&limit=20&mediaType=IMAGE&eventId=event_object_id
```

## 10.2 Get Gallery Asset Details

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery/:assetId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

## 10.3 Generate Upload Signature

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery/upload-signature`

Permission: ACTIVE authorized uploader.

Request:

```json
{
  "fileName": "haldi.jpg",
  "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
  "fileSize": 2048000,
  "mediaType": "IMAGE",
  "eventId": "event_object_id"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "cloudName": "cloudinary_name",
    "apiKey": "cloudinary_api_key",
    "timestamp": 1790000000,
    "signature": "generated_signature",
    "folder": "weddings/wedding_id/gallery"
  }
}
```

The backend generates a signed upload request. The frontend uses it to upload directly to Cloudinary.

The API secret must never be sent to the frontend.

## 10.4 Complete Upload

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery/complete`

Permission: ACTIVE authorized uploader.

Request:

```json
{
  "publicId": "weddings/wedding_id/gallery/file_id",
  "fileName": "haldi.jpg",
  "mediaType": "IMAGE",
  "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
  "fileSize": 2048000,
  "eventId": "event_object_id",
  "visibility": "PRIVATE"
}
```

Business Logic:

1. Verify uploader authorization.
2. Verify the Cloudinary public ID belongs to the wedding's permitted folder.
3. Verify the asset exists using Cloudinary's server-side API.
4. Validate media type and size.
5. Create gallery metadata record.
6. Return the created asset.

The backend must not trust arbitrary Cloudinary URLs or public IDs submitted by the frontend.

## 10.5 Update Gallery Visibility

**PATCH** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery/:assetId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

Request:

```json
{
  "visibility": "PUBLIC"
}
```

## 10.6 Delete Gallery Asset

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/gallery/:assetId`

Permission: ADMIN or MANAGER.

The backend deletes the corresponding Cloudinary asset and updates its MongoDB record.

---

# 11. Public Wedding Website APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/public/wedding`

These APIs allow visitors to access published wedding information without registering or logging in.

## 11.1 Get Public Wedding Website

**GET** `/public/wedding/:token`

Authentication: Not required.

Business Logic:

1. Validate public website token.
2. Check token expiration and revocation.
3. Check wedding website enabled status.
4. Check website visibility.
5. Return only public wedding information.

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "title": "Rahul & Priya Wedding",
    "couple": {
      "partnerOne": "Rahul",
      "partnerTwo": "Priya"
    },
    "weddingDate": "2027-02-15T00:00:00.000Z",
    "location": {
      "venue": "Royal Palace",
      "city": "Bhopal"
    },
    "events": [],
    "template": "traditional"
  }
}
```

Private events, guest information, and workspace member information must never be exposed through this API.

---

# 12. Public Gallery APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/public/gallery`

These APIs provide access to publicly shared wedding photographs.

## 12.1 Get Public Gallery

**GET** `/public/gallery/:token`

Authentication: Not required.

Business Logic:

1. Validate gallery token.
2. Verify token status.
3. Check token expiration.
4. Fetch only PUBLIC and ACTIVE gallery assets.
5. Return paginated gallery data.

## 12.2 Get Public Gallery Asset

**GET** `/public/gallery/:token/:assetId`

Authentication: Not required.

Only publicly accessible assets can be returned.

Private gallery assets must never be exposed through this route.

---

# 13. Public Access Token Management APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/public-access`

These APIs manage access to the wedding website and gallery.

## 13.1 Generate Access Token

**POST** `/weddings/:weddingId/public-access`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Request:

```json
{
  "purpose": "WEDDING_WEBSITE"
}
```

The same endpoint supports:

```json
{
  "purpose": "GALLERY_VIEW"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Access token generated successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": "token_object_id",
    "token": "raw_random_token",
    "purpose": "WEDDING_WEBSITE"
  }
}
```

The raw token is returned only at creation time. Only its hash is stored in MongoDB.

## 13.2 Get Active Tokens

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/public-access`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Token hashes must never be returned.

## 13.3 Revoke Token

**DELETE** `/weddings/:weddingId/public-access/:tokenId`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Rules:

- Website and gallery tokens are independent.
- Only token hashes are stored.
- Raw tokens are returned only when generated.
- Revoked tokens cannot be reused.

---

# 14. Audit Log APIs

**Base Route:** `/api/v1/weddings/:weddingId/audit-logs`

These APIs allow workspace administrators to inspect important activity.

## 14.1 Get Audit Logs

**GET** `/weddings/:weddingId/audit-logs`

Permission: ADMIN only.

Query parameters:

```http
?page=1&limit=20&action=EVENT_CREATED
```

Audit records must be created by backend business logic, not directly by frontend requests.

Audit logs should not be editable through normal application APIs.

---

# 15. Authorization Matrix

| Module | ADMIN | MANAGER | Guest |
|---|---|---|---|
| Wedding | Full access | View and update | Public information only |
| Members | Full access | View members | No access |
| Invitations | Full access | No access | No access |
| Events | Full access | Full access | Public events only |
| Guests | Full access | Full access | No access |
| Gallery | Full access | Full access | Public assets only |
| Public Website | Manage | No access | View |
| Public Tokens | Manage | No access | No access |
| Audit Logs | View | No access | No access |

Cameraman upload-only access is not included in the current role model and requires a separate authorization design.

---

# 16. Middleware and Authorization Flow

Every protected API request must pass through the following process.

```text
Incoming API Request
        |
        v
Extract JWT Cookie
        |
        v
Verify JWT
        |
        v
Get Authenticated User
        |
        v
Extract weddingId
        |
        v
Verify Wedding Exists
        |
        v
Check ACTIVE Membership
        |
        v
Verify Role Permissions
        |
        v
Validate Request Using Zod
        |
        v
Execute Service Logic
        |
        v
Return API Response
```

Public token APIs use token validation instead of normal user authentication.

Authorization must also verify that the requested resource belongs to the same wedding.

---

# 17. API Security Requirements

1. Use HTTPS in production.
2. Store JWT in secure HttpOnly cookies.
3. Apply CSRF protection to cookie-authenticated state-changing requests.
4. Configure CORS for the authorized frontend origin.
5. Validate incoming request bodies using Zod.
6. Apply rate limiting to authentication and token validation APIs.
7. Hash invitation and public access tokens.
8. Never expose password hashes or token hashes.
9. Verify wedding membership for every protected workspace operation.
10. Prevent cross-wedding ObjectId access.
11. Validate uploaded file size, MIME type, and actual file content.
12. Restrict gallery uploads to authorized users.
13. Avoid exposing private gallery storage URLs.
14. Use safe error messages without leaking internal database information.
15. Validate ownership of every referenced document.

---

# 18. API Module Summary

| Module | Endpoints |
|---|---|
| Authentication | Signup, Login, Logout, Me |
| Users | Get Profile, Update Profile, Delete Account |
| Weddings | Create, List, Get, Update, Delete |
| Members | List, Get, Approve, Reject, Update Role, Remove |
| Invitations | Create, List, Validate, Accept, Revoke |
| Events | Create, List, Get, Update, Delete |
| Guests | Create, List, Get, Update, Delete, Bulk Import |
| Gallery | List, Get, Upload Signature, Complete Upload, Update, Delete |
| Public Website | Get Public Wedding |
| Public Gallery | Get Gallery, Get Asset |
| Public Access | Generate, List, Revoke Tokens |
| Audit Logs | Get Activity History |

---

# 19. Express Route Registration

All module routers are registered through a central route file.

Example:

```javascript
import { Router } from "express";

import authRoutes from "../modules/auth/auth.routes.js";
import userRoutes from "../modules/users/user.routes.js";
import weddingRoutes from "../modules/weddings/wedding.routes.js";
import invitationRoutes from "../modules/invitations/invitation.routes.js";
import publicRoutes from "../modules/public-access/public.routes.js";

const router = Router();

router.use("/auth", authRoutes);
router.use("/users", userRoutes);
router.use("/weddings", weddingRoutes);
router.use("/invitations", invitationRoutes);
router.use("/public", publicRoutes);

export default router;
```

In `app.js`:

```javascript
import express from "express";
import apiRoutes from "./routes/index.js";

const app = express();

app.use(express.json());

app.use("/api/v1", apiRoutes);

export default app;
```

Each module is responsible for registering its own subroutes, controllers, and middleware.

---

# 20. Final Architecture Decisions

| Category | Decision |
|---|---|
| API Architecture | REST |
| Base Route | `/api/v1` |
| Frontend | React + Vite |
| Backend | Node.js + Express.js |
| Language | JavaScript |
| Authentication | JWT |
| Session Storage | HttpOnly Cookie |
| Authorization | Membership-based RBAC |
| Validation | Zod |
| Database | MongoDB Atlas |
| ODM | Mongoose |
| Workspace Roles | ADMIN, MANAGER |
| Guest Authentication | Not Required |
| Manager Invitation | Secure Token |
| Website Access | Public Token |
| Gallery Access | Separate Public Token |
| File Storage | Cloudinary |
| Architecture | Modular Monolith |
| Expenses APIs | Not Included |
| Tasks APIs | Not Included |

---

**Document Status:** Initial MERN API Design Complete.

**Next Step:** Backend Implementation Planning.

**Implementation Architecture:** React frontend + Express REST API + MongoDB Atlas + Mongoose, using feature-based modules and server-side authorization.
